course: dictionary
lesson: 10395
title: Tribal and belonging to a group
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Tribal» comes from «tribe», a group of families or communities who share ancestors, language, customs and often land, with their own leaders. In the sentence «The ladies fill the poor man's hair with mud, bang the tribal drums and call every chief of the Tribe», the word «chief» is a clue. Chiefs are leaders, so the drums and the chief belong to a group with its own leader. Tribal means belonging to that kind of group.
explain: Notice the capital letter in «the Tribe». When a word is written with a capital in the middle of a sentence, it is often the name of a particular group. Here it tells you that the people in the story belong to one group that has its own chief.
explain: The word also has a second meaning. «Tribal football fans» are fans who feel very loyal to their own team and do not like the other side. You can test it: swap in your meaning and see if it still makes sense. «Tribal drums» means drums belonging to a tribe, and that fits.
explain: Be respectful when you use this word. Many peoples prefer their own names, such as «nation», «iwi» or «mob». Old books sometimes used tribal to look down on people, and that is wrong. When you read it, ask: is the writer describing a group with respect, or making them sound less important?
fact: Tribal means belonging to a tribe.
fact: A tribe is a group of families or communities who share ancestors, language, customs and often land.
fact: «Tribal» can also mean showing strong loyalty to your own group and dislike of others, as in «tribal football fans».
fact: «Tribal lands», «tribal art» and «tribal leaders» are phrases you might meet in history and geography.
fact: Many Native American nations and Aboriginal and Māori groups prefer their own names, and we should use the names they choose.
exercise: «The ladies bang the tribal drums.» What does tribal mean here? | Loud and very quick | *Belonging to a tribe, a group of families who share ancestors and customs | Made of wood and very old | Played only at weddings
exercise: «Tribal football fans» suggests what? | They play in the rain | They are all related to each other | *Strong loyalty to their own group and dislike of others | They never watch football
exercise: Find and copy one word from «call every chief of the Tribe» that means a leader of a group. | mud | drums | hair | *chief
test: «Tribal leaders guide their people.» What does tribal mean in this sentence? | Made of stone | *Belonging to a tribe | Very tall | Belonging to a school
test: Why does the capital letter in «the Tribe» help you? | It shows the sentence is angry | It means the word is very important in every book | It means the word is a question | *It shows it is the name of a particular group
exam: Many Native American nations prefer their own names. What is the respectful thing to do? | Call them all tribal, because it is a simple word | *Use the name the people choose for themselves | Use the word tribal to make them sound old-fashioned | Never talk about them at all
